<title>MEXICO: Benavides to propose share dividend.</title>
<headline>Benavides to propose share dividend.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican pharmacuetical firm Benavides will propose to shareholders a dividend payment of 0.23 pesos per share in its April 22 annual assembly, a company source said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It has 120.901 million shares. If it is approved, the dividend will be paid in a lump sum at the end of April.</p>
<p>--Jacqueline Lerma, Monterrey newsroom +528 345-7677))</p>
